# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Axial — environment and setup
# Copy this file to .env and fill it in. Without these two values the app runs
# in demo mode only (sample data in your browser, no accounts).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# Only for `npm run seed:demo` (never put this in Vercel or anything prefixed VITE_)
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── Run locally ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   npm install
#   npm run dev            → http://localhost:5173
#   npm test               → unit tests (calculations, rules, CSV import)
#   npm run build          → type-check + production build
#
# ── Database (Supabase) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   1. Create a project at supabase.com. In Database → Extensions enable pg_cron.
#   2. npm i -g supabase && supabase login && supabase link --project-ref YOUR-PROJECT-REF
#   3. supabase db push                       (runs supabase/migrations: tables, RLS, reminder scheduler)
#   4. supabase functions deploy delete-account
#   5. Auth → URL configuration: Site URL = your app URL; add <app>/auth/update-password to redirect URLs.
#   6. Optional sample account: npm run seed:demo  (creates demo@axial.local / Demo-Axial-2026 with rows marked source=demo)
#
# ── Email reminders (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#   In-app reminders are created hourly by pg_cron with no extra setup.
#   For email: get a Resend API key, verify a sending domain, then
#     supabase functions deploy send-email-notifications
#     supabase secrets set RESEND_API_KEY=... EMAIL_FROM="Axial <reminders@yourdomain.com>" CRON_SECRET=<random>
#   and run supabase/email-cron.sql.example in the SQL editor (fill in the placeholders).
#
# ── Deploy (Vercel) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   Import the GitHub repo in Vercel (framework: Vite). Add VITE_SUPABASE_URL and
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY as environment variables. vercel.json handles SPA routing.
#   Then set the Supabase Site URL to the Vercel domain.
